\cf3 An LDL of 168 mg/dL is elevated, particularly at age 69-70. While your healthy lifestyle, normal weight, BP, and sugar are commendable, this LDL level still increases cardiovascular risk. Continuing your diet and exercise is vital. Given your age and LDL, medication, typically a statin, is often advised to significantly lower your long-term cardiovascular risk, even in the absence of other traditional risk factors. (Question: What treatment is suggested for high IDL around 168?My age is 69-70 range. I have high ldl around 168. However, my ldl/hdl ratio is 3.47 and cholesterol /hdl is 5.29. My weight is normal. I go for regular walking and practice yoga. No heart related family history. BP, sugar normal. Do you advise my taking medicine to lower ldl?)\cell \row

