\cf3 Eyelid swelling after heart surgery can be due to several factors. Fluid retention and shifts, common after major surgery, can sometimes manifest locally. Inflammation from surgical positioning or mild irritation during recovery is also possible. While you suspect no allergy, a delayed or mild reaction to medication or environmental factors can't be entirely ruled out. Monitor for redness, pain, vision changes, or worsening swelling, as these could indicate an infection or other issue requiring medical evaluation. (Question: What causes swelling of eyelid after heart surgery?My husband is home recovering from heart surgery. Suddenly one of his eye lids swelled up after dinner. He didn t eat anything new and he has been taking his post surgery medicine for several days, so I didn t think it is from an allergy. Should I worry.)\cell \row

