\cf3 An SGPT of 133 after dengue fever is a common finding, indicating mild liver inflammation from the viral infection. Your normal bilirubin and recovering platelets are positive signs. This elevation often resolves spontaneously as you recover. It's advisable to recheck your liver function tests in 2-4 weeks. Meanwhile, avoid alcohol and unnecessary medications like acetaminophen, and ensure good hydration to support your liver's recovery. (Question: Any suggestion for having SGPT level of 133?My age is 42 and male. I had a dengue fever 10 days back and my platelet count is 95 K. and serum biluribin is.08-1.00. which is in normal lable.. after that one more count of pletelet which is now 1,90,000.00. but my sgpt is quite high is 133. Pls advise.)\cell \row

