\cf3 The green appearance of veins is normal and relates to how light interacts with your skin and blood. Deoxygenated blood in veins is dark red, but your skin absorbs red light and scatters blue-green light, making the veins appear green or blue. This effect is more pronounced with veins closer to the surface. It's common to notice them more with age due to changes in skin translucency or fat layers. (Question: What causes green colored blood veins running across the chest?I'm 57 year old male, 5'6", 150 lbs. Around seven months, I noticed green colored blood veins running ~ horizontally across top of chest with some branching between breast. There's no pain or irritation. It's just something new and unexpected. Is there a known cause?)\cell \row

