\cf3 Divalproex can begin showing effects for acute mania within a few days to a week, with full stabilization taking longer. Titration typically occurs every 1-3 days, guided by clinical response and serum valproate levels. The therapeutic goal is usually a serum level of 50-125 mcg/mL. Initial dosing is often 750 mg/day in divided doses, or 20 mg/kg/day. For a 116 lb (52.6 kg) woman, this would be approximately 1050 mg/day, adjusted as needed to reach the target serum level. (Question: How can severe mania be treated?Yes, my sister is in an acute manic state: pressured speech, grandiosity, paranoia, inappropriate humor, out of touch with reality, etc. She just started on Divalproex, 250 mg. How long will it take to take effect.??How fast can it be titrated up? What s the therapeutic dose for a 69 year old woman of 5 ft, 116 lbs?)\cell \row

