\cf3 A ferritin level of 4 signifies severe iron deficiency. While oral iron pills are standard, they take time to replete stores. Given severe anemia, intravenous (IV) iron infusions are often recommended for faster iron repletion and symptom improvement. Blood transfusions are reserved for critically low hemoglobin levels causing significant symptoms or instability, to rapidly improve oxygen delivery, not primarily to raise ferritin. (Question: Should I undergo a blood transfusion or take an iron pill for low ferritin level?Hi I recently been diagnosed as severely anaemic my ferritin level is at four and I was wondering what should I do them is taking iron pills enough or should I be getting a blood transfusion of some kind or shots or something?)\cell \row

