\cf3 Prednisone, a corticosteroid, reduces airway inflammation, which can alleviate cough and bronchitis symptoms in certain cases. It's often effective for conditions like asthma exacerbations or severe inflammatory bronchitis. However, for typical post-viral acute bronchitis, which is usually self-limiting, prednisone is generally not recommended. Most acute bronchitis is viral, and corticosteroids offer limited benefit, carrying potential side effects. A cough lasting four weeks post-viral infection is common and often resolves without steroid intervention. (Question: Is Prednisone effective in the treatment of cough and bronchitis?I have had an upper respiratory virus and cold with congestion, coughing Itchy irritated throat and malaise. Four weeks later still have some cough and congestion and seems to have settled into Bronchitis. Would a round of Prednisone help to clear this all the way up? Thank you, Rob)\cell \row

