\cf3 Your symptoms of weakness, falls, and seeing bright lights upon standing, coupled with a pulse ox drop, strongly suggest orthostatic hypotension. When you stand, gravity can cause blood to pool in your legs, temporarily reducing blood flow to your heart and brain. This drop in blood pressure to the brain causes your weakness, visual changes, and risk of falling. The pulse ox drop can reflect this temporary decrease in oxygen delivery to your extremities due to reduced circulation. (Question: What causes reduction in pulse Ox while standing?my pulse ox drops upon standing...why? I am 86 and am having spells when I stand I get weak and fall down. I also see bright lights when this happens. I feel good otherwise and have had everything from head to toe checked all normal except my pulse ox drops when I stand.)\cell \row

