\cf3 Post-surgical infections can stem from various factors, including bacteria on the skin entering the wound during or after surgery, or compromised immune response. Despite sterile precautions, this can occur. Regarding your period, it is very common for the menstrual cycle to be disrupted after major surgery. The stress on your body from the procedure, anesthesia, pain medications, and antibiotics can all impact hormonal balance, causing a delayed or missed period. Your cycle should typically normalize in the coming months. (Question: What is the cause of an infection after a tummy tuck and breast lift?I had a tummy tuck and a breast lift. I then developed An infection and they and to go back in and remove all the stitches and change them. I was on antibiotics in hospital two days. I. Have not had a period yet, is this normal?was on period during surgery which was originally oct 31)\cell \row

