\cf3 "Metaline" is likely **Mitotane (Lysodren)**. Yes, Mitotane specifically targets and destroys adrenal cortical cells. If used, it will affect your remaining adrenal gland, potentially causing significant damage or destruction of its cortical tissue. This often leads to adrenal insufficiency, requiring lifelong hormone replacement. Its purpose as a "precautionary measure" (adjuvant therapy) is to eliminate any microscopic residual disease, but this comes with the risk of impacting healthy adrenal function. (Question: Can Metaline destroy the remaining adrenal gland?I had my right adrenal gland removed because of a tumour on the cortex...the histolics show a small spot in the centre of clear cells.not divided..they are tslking about using Metaline? as a precaution measure..will this destroy my one remaining Adrenal Gland??)\cell \row

