\cf3 Your experience strongly suggests Transient Global Amnesia (TGA). This condition causes a sudden, temporary episode of memory loss, typically lasting several hours, where you cannot form new memories (like what happened 5 minutes ago) but retain personal identity and basic knowledge. You generally appear normal to others. While the exact cause isn't always clear, triggers can include stress, physical exertion, or emotional events, often when out of routine. Recovery is usually complete, with no lasting effects. (Question: What causes short-term memory loss for a duration of 8 hours?last Thursday I had a period of 8 hour of short term memory lost. During that time I acted normal and knew basic answers to questions I should know but was unable to remember what I had done 5 minutes earlier. That short term memory lost last for about 8 hours. I was on vacation and out of my daily routine.)\cell \row

