\cf3 Chickenpox scars, often appearing as "holes" or depressions (atrophic scars), can be significantly improved with various treatments. Fractional laser therapy is very effective, stimulating collagen production to resurface the skin. Microneedling can also improve texture and shallow scars. For deeper individual depressions, dermal fillers can temporarily elevate the skin. Chemical peels, subcision, or punch excisions might also be considered depending on the scar type. A dermatologist can assess your specific scars and recommend the most suitable treatment plan. (Question: Q. How to get rid of the chickenpox scars?Hello doctor,I am suffering from chickenpox scars since childhood as it left so many marks and holes on my face. I need some suggestions to get rid of it. Please help.)\cell \row

