\cf3 The sensation of your heart being squeezed, especially with left arm numbness, is a serious concern often indicating reduced blood flow to your heart muscle. This can happen if an artery supplying the heart becomes narrowed or blocked, causing ischemia. The heart muscle, lacking oxygen, signals pain. Numbness in the left arm is a common example of "referred pain," where nerve signals from the heart are interpreted by the brain as coming from the arm. (Question: Why does one feel that the heart is being squeezed?Hi, may I answer your health queries right now? Please type your query here...My heart feels like its being squeezed and my arm goes numb on the left side-Ask a Doctor queries My heart feels like its being squeezed and my arm goes numb on the left side-Ask a Doctor queries)\cell \row

